==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 22~24 seconds<sup>660f~720f</sup>.
*1 [[Doge Dark]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Otta-smack-u]]s spawn after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
*1 [[Li'l Zyclone]] spawns after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[M. Ost]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Hackey]] spawns.
**3 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 3~4 seconds<sup>90f~120f</sup>.
**3 [[Li'l Zyclone]]s spawn, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
**2 [[Li'l Zyclone]]s spawn, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
**6 [[Otta-smack-u]]s spawn, delay 14.67~16.67 seconds<sup>440f~500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage isn't too bad: the Li'l Zyclones give you a stepping stone for you to spam anti M. Ost units like [[Medusa Cat (Rare Cat)|Naga Cat]], [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]] or perhaps [[Masked Yulala (Special Cat)|Spiritual Yulala]]. On higher crown difficulties [[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]] is a necessity to deal with the buffed otters.

==Trivia==
*Like all [[Dawn of the Beginning]] stages except [[Buried Hypocrisy]], Passionate Release's name is the reverse of one from [[Dead End Night]], in this case [[Agape's Cage]] (Passionate Release is freedom, Agape's Cage is entrapment).

